WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
anyone who wants to understand vladimir  putin needs to know the story of what  happened to him one night in east  germany 33 years ago it was december 5  1989 just a few weeks after the berlin  wall fell in east germany communism was  dead although free democratic elections  weren't scheduled until the spring in  the east german city of dredsden  protesters stormed the regional  headquarters of the east german secret  police the stasi completely overrunning  the office then a small group of  protesters reportedly no more than 20  decided to head across the road to the  local headquarters of the soviet secret  service the kgb  russian media later exaggerated the  number of demonstrators to five thousand  putin anticipated the protester his  arrival and called for help from the  soviet military stationed in east  germany to protect the employees in the  office as well as the files they had an  informant in agents they tried to burn  as many of the files as possible and  even broke the furnace but the red army  was not coming to the rescue in his  biography first person putin recalled  being told on the phone we cannot do  anything without orders from moscow and  moscow is silent those words moscow is  silent stayed with them because it  finally dawned on him that the soviet  union had all but disappeared now it was  up to putin to figure out how to get  himself and his kgb colleagues out of  that dangerous situation how could he  stop the crowd from swarming the  building in an interview with the bbc  one of the protesters siegfried dannath  recalled how when the mob approached the  kgb house the guard immediately rushed  inside shortly afterward an officer  emerged quite small agitated that  officer was 37 year old kgb lieutenant  colonel vladimir putin except he didn't  say he was a spy putin said he was a  translator he told the crowd in fluent  german that the property was on soviet  territory according to the protester  putin said to the group don't try to  force your way into this property my  comrades are armed and they're  authorized to use their weapons in an  emergency  putin was bluffing but the mob believed  him and backed away leaving staff and  the sensitive files unscathed  long before vladimir putin became  president of russia he fulfilled his  teenage wish of becoming a kgb agent  inspired by the books he read in films  he watched he spent five years stationed  in the isolated east german city of  dresden from 1985 to 1989. east germany  was important to moscow it was a  satellite state of the soviet union that  sat on the doorstep of nato the western  military alliance we don't have much  information about what kind of work  putin did in dresden he said little  about his work in the 80s other than  speaking about that december day in 1989  what he witnessed was humiliating he saw  the west winning the cold war as the  eastern bloc crumbled under his feet the  atlantic wrote putin's experience in  dresden undoubtedly reinforced his view  of his identity and role as the critical  outsider learning from the mistakes of  others soviet leader mikhail gorbachev  failed to prevent the subsequent  collapse of the soviet union in 1991 one  of the largest and most powerful empires  in history unraveled breaking up into 15  nations leaving russia a shadow of its  former self putin called it the greatest  geopolitical catastrophe of the 20th  century  he later claimed he knew the collapse  was inevitable quote i understood that a  position based on walls and water  barriers cannot exist forever but i  wanted something different to rise in  its place and nothing different was  proposed that's what hurt putin never  rose to the top ranks of the kgb he  remained a mid-level agent on the  periphery in the 90s he left the kgb to  become deputy mayor of st petersburg and  by the late 90s he transferred to moscow  to work in president boris yeltsin's  administration he was picked to lead the  new federal security service which  replaced the kgb and then he was  surprisingly chosen by yeltsin as prime  minister in 1999 he saw how weak russia  had become when president bill clinton  approved airstrikes against serbian  forces in bosnia washington didn't even  consult yeltsin the serbs share deep  ethnic and religious ties with russia  putin's leadership would be very  different from yeltsin's when he took  over as president in 2000 he impressed  clinton's point man on russia strobe  talbot the u.s deputy secretary of state  who wrote in his memoirs that he was  struck by putin's ability to convey  self-control in confidence in a low-key  soft-spoken manner putin's image though  is anything but low-key he's frequently  photographed doing super manly things  like fishing shirtless overpowering  opponents in judo or driving race cars  the macho president has put his tough  image on display for both his fellow  countrymen and the world reinforcing the  image of a strong leader trying to build  up a strong resurgent country in 1999  just before taking office putin stressed  the importance of strengthening the  state writing in an article in the  russian newspaper nizavisimiya guiazieta  russia is in the midst of one of the  most difficult periods in its history  for the first time in the past 200 to  300 years it is facing a real threat of  sliding to the second and possibly even  third echelon of world states we are  running out of time for removing this  threat many believe his actions over the  years have been guided by one principle  to make russia great again  when russia annexed the crimean  peninsula from ukraine in 2014 it led to  a spike in putin's popularity at home  in late on february 23 2022 russia  started attacking targets all over  ukraine why the clearest answer came  from putin himself two days prior to the  attack putin delivered a speech where he  described ukraine as an illegitimate  country that it sits on historically  russian land he views ukraine as a lost  part of russia itself but ukraine  doesn't see it that way it voted  overwhelmingly to establish an  independent state and now seeks to join  nato which putin is determined to block  putin's closest aides today consist of  those from his kgb days or who have  security backgrounds they are believed  to tell him only what he wants to hear  president putin is said to want to  rebuild a sphere of influence in eastern  europe bemoaning the collapse of the  communist order which traumatized him as  a young agent in east germany in this  latest attack on ukraine a russian tank  could be seen flying the soviet flag  officially russia has dismissed the  possibility of reviving the soviet union  putting the story together from start to  finish in just a couple of days was not  easy to pull off it's really important  for me to stay as healthy as possible so  i feel good and can be as productive as  possible  my sponsor by optimizer is mineral rich  supplement magnesium breakthrough aims  to help you beat stress fatigue and  sleep better i have trouble sleeping and  for the past few months i've been taking  magnesium breakthrough myself and i've  noticed that my sleep has gotten a lot  better most magnesium supplements fail  because they're synthetic or use  preservatives when you get all seven  critical forms of magnesium your body  gets a serious upgrade so you feel  better throughout your day to find out  more go to magnesiumbreakthrough.com  newsthink to get a 10 discount be sure  to use the promo code newsthink10 at  checkout you can click my custom link in  the description or pinned comment and  try the powerful effects of magnesium  for yourself thanks for watching for  newsthink i'm cindy palm

